Ultra XR: hand joints (XR_EXT_hand_tracking), a separate aim pose, one tracking space and recentring for the pocketxr
driver. Apply after 0001 and 0002 on upstream commit ee03722885e777462708841223b60affe6873ac2 with: git apply
Copyright 2026, Ultra XR contributors. GPL-3.0-or-later (the new file pocketxr_hands.c carries that SPDX tag; the
changes to Pocket XR's and Monado's BSL-1.0 files are offered under GPL-3.0-or-later too). All of it is linked into
libmonado-service.so only (and PocketFeed.java into the ipc AAR), never into libopenxr_monado.so, the library that
OpenXR applications load.

- drivers/pocketxr/pocketxr_hands.c (new): one xrt_device "Ultra XR hands" with the inputs
  XRT_INPUT_HT_UNOBSTRUCTED_LEFT and _RIGHT, fed by pocketxr_feed_hand / PocketFeed.nativeHand.
- drivers/pocketxr/pocketxr_hmd.c: head, controllers and hands share one tracking origin (before, the builder gave the
  head and each controller its own, 1.6 m up and at (-0.2 or 0.2, 1.3, -0.5)); an origin offset applied to every pose
  (default 1.6 m up) with pocketxr_set_origin_offset and pocketxr_recenter; an aim pose fed apart from the grip
  (pocketxr_feed_controller_aim); the head reports position tracking; devices get default function pointers.
- targets/service-lib/service_target.cpp, ipc PocketFeed.java: nativeHand, nativeConfigureHands, nativeControllerAim,
  nativeSetOriginOffset, nativeRecenter.

